# Ignore everything in this directory (generated HTML, etc.)...
/*
# ...except these pages
!/index.html
!/tractatus.html
!/start.html
# ...the 404 page, which wrangler.jsonc wires to not_found_handling: "404-page"
!/404.html
# ...and the committed agent-skills tree (published by the website deploy)
!/skills
# ...but the rendered skill HTML is derived from the .md — regenerated, not committed
# skills/**/*.html
# ...and the article figures: each is a committed .tex sidecar (the tikz-cd source,
# read back by articles/tikz.lua for the PDF) plus the .svg the markdown references.
# The rest of articles/ stays generated/ignored, so articles/ has to be re-included
# first — a negation inside an excluded directory is otherwise never consulted.
!/articles/
/articles/*
!/articles/images/
!/articles/images/**
# ...and the terminal screencasts: the authored cast sources and their preview
# page (asciinema/), the vendored asciinema player (lib/), and the page loader
# (js/).  All three are source, committed and served by the deploy — the rest of
# this tree is regenerated, so a directory shipped as source has to be
# re-included explicitly.
!/asciinema
!/lib
!/js
# The mtron training corpus is a build product: the extractor writes the corpus, its manifest,
# the verification report, and the verified train/dev split. Regenerated on demand before a run,
# never committed — see docs/skills/mtron/references/unsloth-training-mtron.md §1.
/skills/mtron/assets/mtron_training_dataset*

